# Backlog footprints

`knowledge/backlog-packages.json` remains schema_version 1. Each authored PR
batch declares `touches: ["repo/path.py", "repo/directory/"]`; a package may
provide a default when its batches share one footprint. A batch's explicit
list overrides that default. List substantive source, test, workflow and
rule surfaces; omit routine generated/append-only ledgers to avoid turning
every job into a global lock. Re-author footprints when scope changes.

Paths are relative, slash-normalized and case-insensitive (Windows clone).
A trailing slash denotes a directory and includes all descendants. A file
matches only that file: `backend/capture/` must not match `backend/capture2/`.
Absolute paths, parent traversal and glob syntax are invalid.

New claim comment blocks include a JSON `touches` list, preserving the scope
at claim time. Legacy or malformed footprints resolve through their `batch`
reference, then the claimed issue's authored batch. Unresolvable live claims
block selection with an explicit unknown-footprint reason; never assume
unknown means disjoint. Released/stale claims do not hold files.

`next`, explicit `next --package`, and `claim` use the same overlap check.
Skip any candidate batch touching a live claim's file/directory, continue
to a disjoint batch in the same package, then the next ranked package.
Expose the reason `files overlap an in-flight claim`, holder and paths in
`claims --conflicts`. Claims remain advisory: after publication re-read and
yield to an earlier overlapping claim. `--force` does not steal a live file
claim. No inference from branch names or GitHub assignees.

Pure path/selection logic lives in `backlog_footprints.py`; GitHub command
effects live in `backlog_claim_commands.py` (ADR 001 modular separation).
